    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "text": "Charles Meryon (sometimes Méryon, 23 November 1821 – 14 February 1868) was a French artist who worked almost entirely in etching, as he had colour blindness. Although now little-known in the English-speaking world, he is generally recognised as the most significant etcher of 19th century France.",
      "source": {
        "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
        "title": "Charles Meryon",
        "publisher": "Wikipedia",
        "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Meryon",
        "tier": 5,
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "accessed": "2026-11-26"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "text": "About no other modern etcher, save Whistler, is there an equal consensus of opinion among those whose opinion counts, that he ranks among the great masters of his art.",
